74ex|n|A sharp-pointed tool for picking; -- often used in composition; as, a toothpick; a picklock. ; A heavy iron tool, curved and sometimes pointed at both ends, wielded by means of a wooden handle inserted in the middle, -- used by quarrymen, roadmakers, etc.; also, a pointed hammer used for dressing millstones. ; A pike or spike; the sharp point fixed in the center of a buckler. ; Choice; right of selection; as, to have one's pick. ; That which would be picked or chosen first; the best; as, the pick of the flock. ; A particle of ink or paper imbedded in the hollow of a letter, filling up its face, and occasioning a spot on a printed sheet. ; That which is picked in, as with a pointed pencil, to correct an unevenness in a picture. ; The blow which drives the shuttle, -- the rate of speed of a loom being reckoned as so many picks per minute; hence, in describing the fineness of a fabric, a weft thread; as, so many picks to an inch.	a:xgz,80,3;1p1n,69,3;1giy,57,213;6997,52,3;2bf9,46,47;6cih,45,45;3s8m,40,4;4hij,38,5;4jo7,37,1;69pn,36,1;8qa7,34,16;5wdi,32,4;4j60,31,2;9qk5,30,33;2vtj,26,1~1giy,57,213;3wjj,14,52;2bf9,46,47;6cih,45,45;9qk5,30,33;5fl2,4,27;8qa7,34,16;8tpf,18,10;alsh,5,10;8c3m,19,9;882m,3,8;9pkf,7,6;9hs9,6,6;4hij,38,5;3s8m,40,4	v:1giy,60,262;6cih,47,52;hwt,38,2;1gay,24,1;7pir,19,192;9u2y,18,2;3uir,15,2;2vde,7,3;50qn,2,1;1fr4,1,2~1giy,60,262;7pir,19,192;6cih,47,52;2vde,7,3;9u2y,18,2;1fr4,1,2;3uir,15,2;hwt,38,2;1gay,24,1;50qn,2,1	V:781i,69,11;781f,50,5;2or6,27,4~781i,69,11;781f,50,5;2or6,27,4	n:4jo7,68,9;1giy,67,414;6cih,60,128;47hw,58,8;69pn,46,2;6997,46,2;1zs0,46,4;4j60,41,4;6zol,39,6;39jx,37,4;8c3m,35,27;5bj9,35,11;2fdd,34,3;686e,32,5;2mry,31,147~1giy,67,414;2mry,31,147;6cih,60,128;49do,15,88;2krt,5,82;alrg,5,70;2eui,20,60;2fc0,4,46;3sp6,4,42;9mrs,2,33;3wjj,7,32;6p0c,13,28;8c3m,35,27;3t7w,14,23;9lpv,22,22	N:8r70,56,9;781i,50,3;aj1u,49,625;plg,43,60;1fb4,35,2;a7td,34,10;hk,30,8;6clx,30,3;1eju,30,3;9gvm,25,7;78ku,25,3;a5jv,21,48;5eiv,20,2;2t0i,19,5;hi,18,