75e7|v|To play on a pipe, fife, flute, or other tubular wind instrument of music. ; To call, convey orders, etc., by means of signals on a pipe or whistle carried by a boatswain. ; To emit or have a shrill sound like that of a pipe; to whistle. ; To become hollow in the process of solodifying; -- said of an ingot, as of steel. ; To perform, as a tune, by playing on a pipe, flute, fife, etc.; to utter in the shrill tone of a pipe. ; To call or direct, as a crew, by the boatswain's whistle. ; To furnish or equip with pipes; as, to pipe an engine, or a building.	o:3boy,61,2;2llu,61,37;ao38,59,2;6407,51,1;5jdj,41,2;924u,31,52;amwl,30,2;1jzl,29,3;3yo6,29,2;925x,24,53;22xb,20,1;6cer,20,1;asz5,18,1;375j,18,2;3bp3,18,3~1ot9,7,100;925x,24,53;924u,31,52;2llu,61,37;9259,16,26;4jmr,10,11;amwj,17,6;1d0y,15,5;4uep,5,4;2ne5,11,4;6pwj,13,3;6pto,12,3;1jzl,29,3;3bp3,18,3;3yo6,29,2	s:5p09,106,2;6pb2,77,1;2ppw,68,5;8258,63,2;40gu,49,3;7ket,49,63;1xih,37,1;5vtv,36,3;77kr,28,2;5de4,25,4;8xjk,25,2;6pto,22,6;5ivw,21,3;72im,20,3;3hr6,19,1~7ket,49,63;2my5,10,23;32z2,7,8;6pto,22,6;2ppw,68,5;15v,1,5;9pr3,3,4;5de4,25,4;5vtv,36,3;5ivw,21,3;40gu,49,3;72im,20,3;77kr,28,2;8xjk,25,2;8258,63,2	D:7q2s,50,3;2llu,19,2;82r5,16,1;925x,6,15;9ej3,6,11;2akf,4,1;65c4,4,4;8cwl,2,1~925x,6,15;9ej3,6,11;65c4,4,4;7q2s,50,3;2llu,19,2;82r5,16,1;8cwl,2,1;2akf,4,1
